-- The 2+-module promotion of test/engine_fixtures/return_only_param_dispatch.mdk: the
-- grounding `impl Get (Box a) a` lives in the ENTRY module, and `get1`'s `v` appears
-- only in return position, so `Debug v` grounds only if the impl universe the entry
-- module is checked under contains the entry module's OWN impls.
--
-- `foldModules` never folds a module into its own `accAll`, so every per-module worker
-- must fold `prog` in itself; a driver that passes bare `accAll` rejects this program
-- with `Ambiguous instance for `Debug``. That is why the fixture is here rather than in
-- an engine corpus: `check`, `run` and `build` reach inference through three different
-- drivers, and this shape is what tells them apart.
--
-- EXPECTED VALUE DERIVED BY HAND, not captured: `get1 (Box 42)` is `42 : Int` and
-- `debug` on an Int renders its decimal form, so `main` prints 42.
import lib.rop_own_get.{Box(..), Get, get1}

impl Get (Box a) a where
  get1 (Box x) = x

shown = debug (get1 (Box 42))

main = println shown
